{% block content %}
<main id="main" class="page page-prose spec-body">
  <h1>Start: build a todo app</h1>

  <p>Build a complete local todo application with {{ framework_version }}. The <a href="https://github.com/waaseyaa/waaseyaa-org/blob/main/bin/verify-tutorial.php">fresh-install check</a> extracts the application files displayed here and exercises the application over HTTP. Component tests separately check entity operations and route matching. The <a href="/docs">reference docs</a> come from the same released framework version.</p>

  <p>Waaseyaa is alpha software; APIs still move between releases. The <a href="/docs/specs/stability-charter">stability charter</a> says which surfaces are protected.</p>

  <h2>1. Create the project and site contract</h2>

  <p>You need PHP 8.5 or later, Composer 2, and the SQLite extensions <code>pdo_sqlite</code> and <code>sqlite3</code>. Run these commands in a terminal. The <code>php vendor/bin/waaseyaa</code> form works in PowerShell as well as a POSIX shell.</p>
  <pre><code>composer create-project waaseyaa/waaseyaa my-app {{ framework_version }} --stability=alpha
cd my-app</code></pre>

  <p>The starter version is pinned to this guide. The installer creates your local <code>.env</code> and application secrets. Keep <code>APP_ENV=local</code> and <code>WAASEYAA_DEV_FALLBACK_ACCOUNT=true</code> for this exercise. This single-user example uses development authentication; use sample data and keep the server bound to your own computer.</p>
  <p>Create <code>site.seed.yaml</code> in the project root. The minimal preset supplies the site's baseline contract; the Todo entity below is application-owned.</p>
  <pre><code data-tutorial-file="site.seed.yaml">schema: waaseyaa.site-seed
version: 1
application:
  id: todo-tutorial
  name: Todo Tutorial
  canonical_origin:
    config_key: APP_URL
content_types:
  - id: page
    canonical_route: /pages/{slug}</code></pre>
  <pre><code>php vendor/bin/waaseyaa site:init --preset=minimal --answers=site.seed.yaml --yes --no-interaction</code></pre>
  <p>This records the site contract and generates its verification command. Add the application files in the following steps before running <code>install:init</code>. Create any missing parent directories when saving a file.</p>

  <h2>2. Define the entity</h2>

  <p>One PHP class is one kind of thing your application stores. The class declares everything about itself with attributes: <code>#[ContentEntityType]</code> names the type (and opts into JSON:API with <code>api: true</code>), <code>#[ContentEntityKeys]</code> maps logical keys to fields, and each <code>#[Field]</code> marks a public typed property as a persistable field. Field types are inferred from the PHP property types.</p>

  <p>Every field also declares who may read it. Waaseyaa is deny-by-default at the field level too: a field without a read level is internal and application code cannot read it. That is a deliberate property of the framework, not a tutorial inconvenience; see <a href="/docs/specs/field-access">field-access.md</a>.</p>

  <p>Create <code>src/Entity/Todo.php</code>:</p>

  <pre><code data-tutorial-file="src/Entity/Todo.php">&lt;?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Entity;

use Waaseyaa\Entity\Attribute\ContentEntityKeys;
use Waaseyaa\Entity\Attribute\ContentEntityType;
use Waaseyaa\Entity\Attribute\Field;
use Waaseyaa\Entity\ContentEntityBase;
use Waaseyaa\Entity\FieldReadLevel;

#[ContentEntityType(id: 'todo', label: 'Todo', api: true)]
#[ContentEntityKeys(label: 'title')]
final class Todo extends ContentEntityBase
{
    #[Field(label: 'Title', required: true, read: FieldReadLevel::Public)]
    public string $title = '';

    #[Field(label: 'Completed', read: FieldReadLevel::Public)]
    public bool $completed = false;

    #[Field(label: 'Priority', read: FieldReadLevel::Public)]
    public string $priority = 'normal';

    public function isCompleted(): bool
    {
        return (bool) $this->get('completed');
    }

    public function toggleCompleted(): static
    {
        return $this->set('completed', !$this->isCompleted());
    }
}</code></pre>

  <p>Register it in <code>config/entity-types.php</code>. Because the class carries its own metadata, registration is one line:</p>

  <pre><code data-tutorial-file="config/entity-types.php">&lt;?php

declare(strict_types=1);

use Waaseyaa\Entity\EntityType;

return [
    EntityType::fromClass(\App\Entity\Todo::class),
];</code></pre>

  <p>The installation step below creates the table and activates configuration after all application files are in place.</p>

  <h2>3. Routes and a typed controller</h2>

  <p>A service provider registers routes. <code>entityParameter('todo', 'todo')</code> marks <code>{todo}</code> as an entity segment: the framework loads the row and passes a <code>Todo</code> instance into an action parameter typed as <code>Todo</code>. Unknown or unreadable ids become a 404 before your code runs. Every route requires <code>manage todos</code>, which the local development account holds. The <code>csrfExempt()</code> setting is only for this local exercise; real applications also require CSRF protection.</p>

  <p>Create <code>src/Provider/TodoServiceProvider.php</code>:</p>

  <pre><code data-tutorial-file="src/Provider/TodoServiceProvider.php">&lt;?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Provider;

use Waaseyaa\Foundation\ServiceProvider\ServiceProvider;
use Waaseyaa\Routing\RouteBuilder;
use Waaseyaa\Routing\WaaseyaaRouter;

final class TodoServiceProvider extends ServiceProvider
{
    public function register(): void {}

    public function routes(
        WaaseyaaRouter $router,
        \Waaseyaa\Entity\EntityTypeManager $entityTypeManager,
    ): void {
        $router->addRoute('todo.list', RouteBuilder::create('/todos')
            ->controller('App\Controller\TodoController::list')
            ->methods('GET')
            ->requirePermission('manage todos')
            ->build());

        $router->addRoute('todo.create', RouteBuilder::create('/todos')
            ->controller('App\Controller\TodoController::create')
            ->methods('POST')
            ->requirePermission('manage todos')
            ->csrfExempt()
            ->build());

        $router->addRoute('todo.toggle', RouteBuilder::create('/todos/{todo}/toggle')
            ->controller('App\Controller\TodoController::toggle')
            ->entityParameter('todo', 'todo')
            ->methods('POST')
            ->requirePermission('manage todos')
            ->csrfExempt()
            ->build());

        $router->addRoute('todo.delete', RouteBuilder::create('/todos/{todo}/delete')
            ->controller('App\Controller\TodoController::delete')
            ->entityParameter('todo', 'todo')
            ->methods('POST')
            ->requirePermission('manage todos')
            ->csrfExempt()
            ->build());
    }
}</code></pre>

  <p>In <code>composer.json</code>, append <code>"App\\Provider\\TodoServiceProvider"</code> to the existing <code>extra.waaseyaa.providers</code> array. Preserve every existing entry, including the provider generated by <code>site:init</code>. Do not replace the rest of the manifest.</p>

  <p>Typed entity arguments also require an entity access policy. Create <code>src/Access/TodoAccessPolicy.php</code>. The attribute makes this policy discoverable; it grants Todo access only to accounts with <code>manage todos</code>. This entity has public fields and no protected-read policy. For entities with protected fields, follow the additional policy contract in <a href="/docs/specs/field-access">field access</a>.</p>
  <pre><code data-tutorial-file="src/Access/TodoAccessPolicy.php">&lt;?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Access;

use Waaseyaa\Access\AccessPolicyInterface;
use Waaseyaa\Access\AccessResult;
use Waaseyaa\Access\AccountInterface;
use Waaseyaa\Access\Gate\PolicyAttribute;
use Waaseyaa\Entity\EntityInterface;

#[PolicyAttribute(entityType: 'todo')]
final class TodoAccessPolicy implements AccessPolicyInterface
{
    public function appliesTo(string $entityTypeId): bool
    {
        return $entityTypeId === 'todo';
    }

    public function access(EntityInterface $entity, string $operation, AccountInterface $account): AccessResult
    {
        return in_array($operation, ['view', 'update', 'delete'], true)
            &amp;&amp; $account->hasPermission('manage todos')
            ? AccessResult::allowed('Account may manage todos.')
            : AccessResult::neutral('Todo permission required.');
    }

    public function createAccess(string $entityTypeId, string $bundle, AccountInterface $account): AccessResult
    {
        return $account->hasPermission('manage todos')
            ? AccessResult::allowed('Account may create todos.')
            : AccessResult::neutral('Todo permission required.');
    }
}</code></pre>

  <p>Persistence goes through the entity repository: <code>create()</code> builds a new, unsaved entity with defaults applied, <code>save()</code> inserts or updates, <code>find()</code> loads by id, <code>findBy([])</code> returns everything, <code>delete()</code> removes one entity. Create <code>src/Controller/TodoController.php</code>:</p>

  <pre><code data-tutorial-file="src/Controller/TodoController.php">&lt;?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Controller;

use App\Entity\Todo;
use Symfony\Component\HttpFoundation\RedirectResponse;
use Symfony\Component\HttpFoundation\Request;
use Symfony\Component\HttpFoundation\Response;
use Twig\Environment;
use Waaseyaa\Entity\EntityTypeManagerInterface;

final class TodoController
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly EntityTypeManagerInterface $entityTypeManager,
        private readonly Environment $twig,
    ) {}

    public function list(): Response
    {
        $repository = $this->entityTypeManager->getRepository('todo');
        $todos = $repository->findBy([]);

        $html = $this->twig->render('todo/list.html.twig', [
            'todos' => $todos,
            'pending' => array_values(array_filter($todos, fn (Todo $t) => !$t->isCompleted())),
            'completed' => array_values(array_filter($todos, fn (Todo $t) => $t->isCompleted())),
        ]);

        return new Response($html);
    }

    public function create(Request $request): Response
    {
        $title = trim((string) $request->request->get('title', ''));
        if ($title === '') {
            return new RedirectResponse('/todos');
        }

        $repository = $this->entityTypeManager->getRepository('todo');
        $todo = $repository->create([
            'title' => $title,
            'completed' => false,
            'priority' => $request->request->get('priority', 'normal'),
        ]);
        $repository->save($todo);

        return new RedirectResponse('/todos');
    }

    public function toggle(Todo $todo): Response
    {
        $todo->toggleCompleted();
        $this->entityTypeManager->getRepository('todo')->save($todo);

        return new RedirectResponse('/todos');
    }

    public function delete(Todo $todo): Response
    {
        $this->entityTypeManager->getRepository('todo')->delete($todo);

        return new RedirectResponse('/todos');
    }
}</code></pre>

  <h2>4. Add the complete template</h2>
  <p>Create <code>templates/todo/list.html.twig</code>. Twig escapes the titles when rendering them. Each form submits to one of the routes above.</p>
  <pre><code data-tutorial-file="templates/todo/list.html.twig">{% apply escape('html') %}{% verbatim %}<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>My todos</title></head>
<body>
  <main>
    <h1>My todos</h1>
    <form method="post" action="/todos">
      <label>Title <input name="title" required></label>
      <label>Priority <select name="priority"><option value="normal">Normal</option><option value="high">High</option></select></label>
      <button type="submit">Add todo</button>
    </form>
    {% for heading, items in {'Pending': pending, 'Completed': completed} %}
      <section aria-label="{{ heading }}">
        <h2>{{ heading }}</h2>
        <ul>
        {% for todo in items %}
          <li data-todo-id="{{ todo.id() }}">
            <span>{{ todo.get('title') }}</span> ({{ todo.get('priority') }})
            <form method="post" action="/todos/{{ todo.id() }}/toggle"><button type="submit">{{ todo.isCompleted() ? 'Mark pending' : 'Complete' }}</button></form>
            <form method="post" action="/todos/{{ todo.id() }}/delete"><button type="submit">Delete</button></form>
          </li>
        {% else %}
          <li>No todos here.</li>
        {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </section>
    {% endfor %}
  </main>
</body>
</html>{% endverbatim %}{% endapply %}</code></pre>

  <h2>5. Install, verify, and run</h2>

  <pre><code>composer dump-autoload
php vendor/bin/waaseyaa install:init
php vendor/bin/waaseyaa optimize:manifest
composer site-verify
php vendor/bin/waaseyaa serve --host=127.0.0.1</code></pre>

  <p><code>install:init</code> applies migrations, creates entity tables, and activates configuration. <code>composer site-verify</code> checks the generated site contract. Stop and fix any reported error before serving. The single-worker PHP development server is sufficient for this exercise; applications needing concurrent requests can use the starter's FrankenPHP runtime.</p>

  <p>Open <code>http://127.0.0.1:8080/todos</code>. Add a todo and see it under Pending. Click Complete and see it under Completed. Click Mark pending, refresh the page to check persistence, then Delete. An unknown todo URL should return 404. Stop the server with Ctrl+C.</p>

  <h2>6. Before exposing an API</h2>

  <p>The entity's <code>api: true</code> declaration opts it into <code>/api/todo</code>, subject to the same entity access policy. Development authentication is not evidence of production readiness. Before sharing the app, restore CSRF protection, disable development authentication, and assign <code>manage todos</code> only to the intended authenticated users. Read <a href="/docs/specs/access-control">access control</a> and <a href="/docs/specs/jsonapi">JSON:API</a>.</p>

